    {
      "id": "claim_c8bdcdd80266405f9c01b5e463598303",
      "statement": "The client is a deliberate fat-client SPA: long-lived sessions make startup time less critical, gadget sandboxing requires client-side execution, a clean API boundary supports alternative clients, and SPA is easier to reason about.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7fa85f5952ecafa4796e2ac8547009e0a9b4db3b74d7f237a38d64a9cb87169:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd9ddbb1604e440dadd6d9c2e5b7090c",
      "statement": "WebSocket connection management lives in module-level globals rather than React effects, because StrictMode's double-invoke would create and discard redundant connections and disconnect handling could end up with two connections fighting; subscribers (a plain callback Set) are notified on stub/connection-state changes and AppWithConnection mirrors them into React state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L188-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24b492fbff8eeab31bb89fb0d8bb949a85d108cd0d5fcf3e5ba3d4bd33ed5525:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L47-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ea8ab8ead05eca06f6107625669567d17c14182f69ef3f5b828a7a46f6fd416:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4de1e5b80cdd46d3a81c8a19254e2679",
      "statement": "Reconnect uses jittered backoff starting at 1s doubling to a 10s cap, skipping the first backoff when the dying connection had been up a while; each candidate must answer a ping() probe within 20s before being published, because capnweb queues sends while a socket is CONNECTING so an unproven stub looks fine until everything pipelined onto it fails at once.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L60-L136",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7cae496cf9a6f1fced178f63fc1b3fdcf057a60a81e4d6904d58d7bec9a10d52:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd640ca32f91434cb0b183d066600379",
      "statement": "On connection loss the module publishes an RpcPromise wrapping the reconnect future instead of a stub: the dead stub stops being reachable immediately and calls pipelined onto the unresolved promise are delivered in order once it resolves, so out-of-outage work waits for the replacement instead of failing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L138-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:050420bfc806171868c8e2e7e7572e9ab69458d2824b20fbe5ebe3acd3eb205d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_467ac8ea93a04c0cab315d5589b7dc2e",
      "statement": "Passive close detection misses sockets killed during laptop sleep or tab throttling, so visibilitychange and online events trigger a wake probe (10s timeout, only after at least 15s since the last proof); a failed probe disposes the suspect stub, triggering the same recovery path with its skip-first-backoff behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L155-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c94c3fd2066f0ca3901627ef6857f9215d4c4607cb45dc7acbb8a2437dcd5490:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
